{"candidate_id": "cand-factcrescendo-0006", "factchecker": "factcrescendo.com", "factcheck_article": "https://english.factcrescendo.com/2021/02/08/video-from-nepal-viral-as-glacier-breaking-off-in-uttarakhands-chamoli/", "social_url": "https://www.instagram.com/tv/CJ4osaYhmch/", "media_url": "https://www.instagram.com/tv/CJ4osaYhmch/", "eligibility_status": "UNRESOLVED", "rejection_reason": "Manually rejected: this post is the TRUE original the article cites as evidence via reverse image search, not the misinformation -- judge got the claim direction backwards.", "ground_truth_claim": "The caption text itself makes a specific false assertion about being from Chamoli, Uttarakhand. The post's own claim is that the video shows an avalanche at Kapuche Glacier Lake in Nepal (specifically stating it as 'Lowest altitude glacier lake in world'), which contradicts Fact Crescendo\u2019s conclusion.", "ground_truth_label": "False", "claim_type": "provenance", "language": "en", "media_type": null, "history": [{"status": "DISCOVERED", "at": "2026-08-18T10:02:22.019472+00:00", "note": "created"}, {"status": "SOCIAL_REFERENCE_FOUND", "at": "2026-08-18T10:02:22.019801+00:00", "note": "Recovered via mass_source_factcrescendo.py sitemap crawl."}, {"status": "MEDIA_RETRIEVABLE", "at": "2026-08-18T10:02:22.020029+00:00", "note": "uploader=Perspicacious Naren, has_caption=True"}, {"status": "ELIGIBLE", "at": "2026-08-18T10:02:31.204089+00:00", "note": "llama3.2 judge (confidence=0.80): The post's caption directly claims the video is from Kapuche Glacier Lake (Nepal), while fact-check article concludes it was actually an avalanche in Nepal on January 11th.. NOT yet human/manual-reviewed."}, {"status": "UNRESOLVED", "at": "2026-08-18T10:22:38.951170+00:00", "note": "Manually rejected -- judge got the claim direction backwards. Real caption: \"Here comes full video of huge avalanche, had to spend overnight at Kapuche lake (Lowest altitude glacier lake in the world)...\" -- accurately describes the video as being at Kapuche Lake, Nepal, with no mention of Chamoli/Uttarakhand/India at all. The article confirms this exact post (uploader, caption wording match near-verbatim) is the TRUE ORIGINAL the article used via reverse image search to debunk a SEPARATE, different post claiming the same footage showed \"glacier breaking off in Uttarakhand's Chamoli\" -- the classic cited-as-evidence-of-the-true-original pattern this whole pipeline exists to filter out. The judge inverted this, treating the accurate Nepal caption as itself a false claim."}]}
